/-!
# Every unary postprocessor fails on an eight-element E3352 model

This covers `x □ y = u (x ◇ y)` for arbitrary unary magma terms `u`.
It does not exclude arbitrary binary terms, so it does not settle a definability row.
All finite checks use kernel `decide`.
-/

